# Verdict

What the kernel said about a proof document, and what the factory accepts.

The kernel is the judge: `largo prove --kernel <document> --json` (or `largo check
--kernel`, which prints the same report) checks every block in order and stops
at the first that does not check. This module reads that report and applies the
ACCEPTANCE POLICY on top of it, which is fixed and is not anything an agent can
edit:

- every block of the assembled document checked;
- the factory's closing `Check <proof>.` printed exactly `<proof> : <goal>`, so the
  theorem has the statement's goal as its type;
- the factory's closing `Print Axioms <proof>.` reports a closure inside
  `propext`, `Quot_sound` and `Classical_choice` — Lean's three axioms, under the
  spellings the LOGOS kernel prints;
- and, before any of that, the submission passed `submission.lg`'s reading and
  every name it declares was free (see `nameProbeVerdict`).

There are exactly four outcomes. `verified`: the policy holds. `rejected`: the
kernel refused a block, or the submission was refused before the kernel saw it;
the block and the error go back to the model. `admitted_axiom`: everything
checked, but the proof rests on an axiom outside the three, so it is progress
modulo that axiom (a decomposition's child lemma), never a proof. `infrastructure`:
the run itself failed — a deadline, a report that is not a report — which is
nobody's mathematical fault and is retried rather than blamed on the attempt.

The recorded reports below were produced by `largo 0.11.0` on the documents in
`tests/fixtures/kernel/`; every classification test reads one of them.

Import Wire.
Import Shared.
Import Submission.

## Note
The axioms an accepted proof may rest on, as the kernel spells them.

## To allowedAxioms () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["propext", "Quot_sound", "Classical_choice"].

## Note
A kernel report, read: whether the document checked, each block's output in
order, the first refused block (`0` when the kernel names none — a document that
does not even parse is refused whole), and the kernel's error.

## A KernelReport has:
    a checked, which is Bool.
    an outputs, which is Seq of Text.
    a failedBlock, which is Int.
    an error, which is Text.

## Note
The shape of `largo … --kernel --json`'s report. It is read OPEN, so a later
`largo` that adds a field still reads; every field named here must be there.

## To kernelReportShape () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["blocks:array", "checked:bool", "error:opttext", "failed_block:optint", "file:text", "surface:text"].

## Note
A kernel report read from what `largo` printed, or why it is not one. The blocks
must be numbered 1, 2, 3, … with a text output each, and the surface must be the
kernel's document door.

## To parseKernelReport (stdout: Text) -> Result of KernelReport and Text:
    Inspect parseStrict(trim(stdout)):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error "the report is not JSON: " + e.
        When Ok (v):
            Let problem be openShapeProblem(v, kernelReportShape()).
            If problem is not equal to "":
                Return a new Err with error "the report is not a kernel report: " + problem.
            Let surface be textAt(v, "surface").
            If surface is not equal to "kernel_document":
                Return a new Err with error "the report's surface is {surface}, not kernel_document".
            Let mutable outputs be a new Seq of Text.
            Let mutable expected be 1.
            Inspect jsonGet(v, "blocks"):
                When JArr (elems):
                    Repeat for b in elems:
                        If openShapeProblem(b, ["block:int", "output:text"]) is not equal to "":
                            Return a new Err with error "block entry {expected} of the report is malformed".
                        Let numbered be intAt(b, "block").
                        If numbered is not equal to expected:
                            Return a new Err with error "the report numbers block {numbered} where {expected} belongs".
                        Push textAt(b, "output") to outputs.
                        Set expected to expected + 1.
                Otherwise:
                    Return a new Err with error "the report has no block list".
            Return a new Ok with value (a new KernelReport with checked boolAt(v, "checked") and outputs outputs and failedBlock intAt(v, "failed_block") and error textAt(v, "error")).
    Return a new Err with error "unreadable report".

## Note
The axioms a `Print Axioms <name>.` output names, or why the output is not that
report for that name. The kernel prints `'n' depends on no axioms` or
`'n' depends on axioms: [a, b]`.

## To axiomsOf (output: Text, name: Text) -> Result of Seq of Text and Text:
    Let nothingSaid be "'" + name + "' depends on no axioms".
    If output is equal to nothingSaid:
        Return a new Ok with value (a new Seq of Text).
    Let lead be "'" + name + "' depends on axioms: [".
    If startsWith(output, lead) and endsWith(output, "]"):
        Let inner be removeSuffix(removePrefix(output, lead), "]").
        Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
        Repeat for part in split(inner, ","):
            If trim(part) is not equal to "":
                Push trim(part) to out.
        Return a new Ok with value out.
    Return a new Err with error "`{output}` is not the axiom report of {name}".

## Note
The axioms of `axioms` that the policy does not allow, in the order given.

## To disallowedAxioms (axioms: Seq of Text) -> Seq of Text:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for a in axioms:
        If allowedAxioms() contains a is equal to false:
            Push a to out.
    Return out.

## Note
A verdict for a run that failed for reasons of its own.

## To infrastructureVerdict (why: Text) -> Verdict:
    Return newVerdict("infrastructure", 0, why, [], "the check itself did not complete; the attempt is retried, not blamed").

## Note
The verdict on one run of `largo prove --kernel <document> --json`: its exit
status, what it printed, and whether its deadline stopped it, for the theorem
`proofName` that must have type `goalName`.

`largo` exits 0 exactly when the document checked and 1 when a block was refused,
and a run whose exit disagrees with its own report is an infrastructure failure,
never a verdict.

## To kernelVerdict (exitCode: Int, stdout: Text, timedOut: Bool, proofName: Text, goalName: Text) -> Verdict:
    If timedOut:
        Return infrastructureVerdict("largo ran past its deadline").
    Inspect parseKernelReport(stdout):
        When Err (e):
            Return infrastructureVerdict("largo exited {exitCode}; " + e).
        When Ok (report):
            If report's checked is equal to false:
                If exitCode is not equal to 1:
                    Return infrastructureVerdict("the report says the document did not check, but largo exited {exitCode}").
                Return newVerdict("rejected", report's failedBlock, report's error, [], "the kernel refused the document").
            If exitCode is not equal to 0:
                Return infrastructureVerdict("the report says the document checked, but largo exited {exitCode}").
            Let n be length of report's outputs.
            If n is less than 2:
                Return newVerdict("rejected", n, "the document has no closing checks", [], "the factory's closing checks did not run as written").
            Let typed be item (n - 1) of report's outputs.
            If typed is not equal to proofName + " : " + goalName:
                Return newVerdict("rejected", n - 1, "`Check {proofName}.` printed `{typed}`, not `{proofName} : {goalName}`", [], "the proof does not have the statement's goal as its type").
            Inspect axiomsOf(item n of report's outputs, proofName):
                When Err (e):
                    Return newVerdict("rejected", n, e, [], "the factory's closing checks did not run as written").
                When Ok (axioms):
                    Let outside be disallowedAxioms(axioms).
                    If length of outside is equal to 0:
                        Return newVerdict("verified", 0, "", axioms, "every block checked; the proof rests on " + axiomPhrase(axioms) + ", within propext, Quot_sound and Classical_choice").
                    Return newVerdict("admitted_axiom", 0, "", axioms, "every block checked, but the proof rests on " + join(outside, ", ") + ", outside propext, Quot_sound and Classical_choice").
    Return infrastructureVerdict("unreadable run").

## Note
How a list of axioms reads in a verdict's detail.

## To axiomPhrase (axioms: Seq of Text) -> Text:
    If length of axioms is equal to 0:
        Return "no axioms".
    Return join(axioms, ", ").

## Note
What a name probe found: `bound` when the name already exists, `free` when the
kernel answered that it is unbound, and `unknown` when the run answered anything
else — which is not evidence either way.

## To probeOutcome (exitCode: Int, stdout: Text, name: Text) -> Text:
    Inspect parseKernelReport(stdout):
        When Err (e):
            Return "unknown".
        When Ok (report):
            If report's checked and exitCode is equal to 0:
                Return "bound".
            If report's checked is equal to false and report's error is equal to "Kernel error: Unbound variable: " + name:
                Return "free".
            Return "unknown".
    Return "unknown".

## Note
The verdict the name probes add, or `none` when every declared name was free.
`names` and `outcomes` are parallel: the name, and what its probe found. `what` is
the document whose names were probed and `boundBy` what they were probed against,
so the refusal says which.

## To nameProbeVerdict (what: Text, boundBy: Text, names: Seq of Text, outcomes: Seq of Text) -> Option of Verdict:
    Repeat for i from 1 to length of names:
        If item i of outcomes is equal to "bound":
            Return some newVerdict("rejected", 0, "the {what} declares {item i of names}, which {boundBy} already binds", [], "a {what} may only add new names").
    Repeat for i from 1 to length of names:
        If item i of outcomes is not equal to "free":
            Return some infrastructureVerdict("the probe of {item i of names} did not answer").
    Return none.

## Note
The verdict on a submission that `submission.lg` refused before the kernel ran.

## To refusedSubmissionVerdict (problems: Seq of Text) -> Verdict:
    Return newVerdict("rejected", 0, join(problems, "; "), [], "the submission was refused before the kernel saw it").

## Note
Whether a proof document is bound to an accepted statement: the statement's
recorded hash is the hash of its document, and the proof document begins with
that document exactly as `assembleProofDocument` places it.

## To boundToStatement (statement: Statement, document: Text) -> Bool:
    If sha256Hex(statement's document) is not equal to statement's sha256:
        Return false.
    Return startsWith(document, trimEnd(statement's document) + "\n\n/-! ## Submission -/\n\n").

## Note
What `largo prove --kernel <fixture>.lg --json` printed for each document in
`tests/fixtures/kernel/`, copied byte for byte from the `<fixture>.prove.json`
recordings (without the final newline `println` adds). `largo check --kernel
--json` printed the same bytes for every one. The live test at the end of this
file holds each copy to its recording, so the two cannot drift apart.

## To recordedReport (fixture: Text) -> Text:
    If fixture is equal to "verified":
        Return "{{\"blocks\":[{{\"block\":1,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":2,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":3,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":4,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":5,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":6,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":7,\"output\":\"proof_of_goal : goal\"}},{{\"block\":8,\"output\":\"'proof_of_goal' depends on no axioms\"}}],\"checked\":true,\"error\":null,\"failed_block\":null,\"file\":\"verified.lg\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}".
    If fixture is equal to "rejected":
        Return "{{\"blocks\":[],\"checked\":false,\"error\":\"Tactic error: step 2 (`rfl`): `rfl` does not apply: Nat_add Zero n and n do not convert\\nin the goal\\nn : Nat\\n⊢ Eq Nat (Nat_add Zero n) n\",\"failed_block\":4,\"file\":\"rejected.lg\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}".
    If fixture is equal to "admitted_axiom":
        Return "{{\"blocks\":[{{\"block\":1,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":2,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":3,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":4,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":5,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":6,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":7,\"output\":\"proof_of_goal : goal\"}},{{\"block\":8,\"output\":\"'proof_of_goal' depends on axioms: [zero_add_axiom]\"}}],\"checked\":true,\"error\":null,\"failed_block\":null,\"file\":\"admitted_axiom.lg\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}".
    If fixture is equal to "parse_error":
        Return "{{\"blocks\":[],\"checked\":false,\"error\":\"Parse error: Expected `[names | names …]`, found [ | k ih; rfl\",\"failed_block\":null,\"file\":\"parse_error.lg\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}".
    If fixture is equal to "shadowed":
        Return "{{\"blocks\":[{{\"block\":1,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":2,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":3,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":4,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":5,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":6,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":7,\"output\":\"proof_of_goal : goal\"}},{{\"block\":8,\"output\":\"'proof_of_goal' depends on no axioms\"}}],\"checked\":true,\"error\":null,\"failed_block\":null,\"file\":\"shadowed.lg\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}".
    If fixture is equal to "classical":
        Return "{{\"blocks\":[{{\"block\":1,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":2,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":3,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":4,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":5,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":6,\"output\":\"proof_of_goal : goal\"}},{{\"block\":7,\"output\":\"'proof_of_goal' depends on axioms: [Classical_choice, Quot_sound, propext]\"}}],\"checked\":true,\"error\":null,\"failed_block\":null,\"file\":\"classical.lg\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}".
    If fixture is equal to "probe_bound":
        Return "{{\"blocks\":[{{\"block\":1,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":2,\"output\":\"\"}},{{\"block\":3,\"output\":\"goal : Prop\"}}],\"checked\":true,\"error\":null,\"failed_block\":null,\"file\":\"probe_bound.lg\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}".
    If fixture is equal to "probe_free":
        Return "{{\"blocks\":[],\"checked\":false,\"error\":\"Kernel error: Unbound variable: succ_step\",\"failed_block\":3,\"file\":\"probe_free.lg\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}".
    Return "".

## Note
The exit status `largo` ended each recorded run with.

## To recordedExit (fixture: Text) -> Int:
    If fixture is equal to "verified":
        Return 0.
    If fixture is equal to "rejected":
        Return 1.
    If fixture is equal to "admitted_axiom":
        Return 0.
    If fixture is equal to "parse_error":
        Return 1.
    If fixture is equal to "shadowed":
        Return 0.
    If fixture is equal to "classical":
        Return 0.
    If fixture is equal to "probe_bound":
        Return 0.
    If fixture is equal to "probe_free":
        Return 1.
    Return 0 - 1.

## Test: a checked report reads block by block

Inspect parseKernelReport(recordedReport("verified")):
    When Ok (r):
        Expect that r's checked is equal to true.
        Expect that length of r's outputs is equal to 8.
        Expect that item 7 of r's outputs is equal to "proof_of_goal : goal".
        Expect that item 8 of r's outputs is equal to "'proof_of_goal' depends on no axioms".
        Expect that r's failedBlock is equal to 0.
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "no error".

## Test: a refused report keeps its block and its error

Inspect parseKernelReport(recordedReport("rejected")):
    When Ok (r):
        Expect that r's checked is equal to false.
        Expect that r's failedBlock is equal to 4.
        Expect that r's outputs is equal to [].
        Expect that r's error is equal to "Tactic error: step 2 (`rfl`): `rfl` does not apply: Nat_add Zero n and n do not convert\nin the goal\nn : Nat\n⊢ Eq Nat (Nat_add Zero n) n".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "no error".

## Test: the axiom report reads both of its forms

Inspect axiomsOf("'p' depends on no axioms", "p"):
    When Ok (xs):
        Expect that xs is equal to [].
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "no error".
Inspect axiomsOf("'p' depends on axioms: [Classical_choice, Quot_sound, propext]", "p"):
    When Ok (xs):
        Expect that xs is equal to ["Classical_choice", "Quot_sound", "propext"].
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "no error".
Inspect axiomsOf("'q' depends on no axioms", "p"):
    When Ok (xs):
        Expect that xs is equal to ["refused"].
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "`'q' depends on no axioms` is not the axiom report of p".

## Test: only Lean's three axioms are allowed, under the kernel's spellings

Expect that disallowedAxioms(["Classical_choice", "Quot_sound", "propext"]) is equal to [].
Expect that disallowedAxioms(["collatz_lemma", "propext"]) is equal to ["collatz_lemma"].
Expect that disallowedAxioms(["Classical.choice", "Quot.sound"]) is equal to ["Classical.choice", "Quot.sound"].
Expect that disallowedAxioms(["sorryAx"]) is equal to ["sorryAx"].

## Test: a correct proof is verified

Let v be kernelVerdict(recordedExit("verified"), recordedReport("verified"), false, "proof_of_goal", "goal").
Expect that v's kind is equal to "verified".
Expect that v's axioms is equal to [].
Expect that v's detail is equal to "every block checked; the proof rests on no axioms, within propext, Quot_sound and Classical_choice".

## Test: a classical proof is verified with the axioms it rests on

Let v be kernelVerdict(recordedExit("classical"), recordedReport("classical"), false, "proof_of_goal", "goal").
Expect that v's kind is equal to "verified".
Expect that v's axioms is equal to ["Classical_choice", "Quot_sound", "propext"].

## Test: a wrong proof is rejected with the kernel's block and error

Let v be kernelVerdict(recordedExit("rejected"), recordedReport("rejected"), false, "proof_of_goal", "goal").
Expect that v's kind is equal to "rejected".
Expect that v's block is equal to 4.
Expect that v's error contains "`rfl` does not apply: Nat_add Zero n and n do not convert".
Expect that blockText(assembleProofDocument(fixtureStatement(), "Theorem proof_of_goal : goal := by intro n; rfl.", "proof_of_goal"), v's block) is equal to "Theorem proof_of_goal : goal := by intro n; rfl.".

## Test: a document that does not parse is rejected whole

Let v be kernelVerdict(recordedExit("parse_error"), recordedReport("parse_error"), false, "proof_of_goal", "goal").
Expect that v's kind is equal to "rejected".
Expect that v's block is equal to 0.
Expect that v's error is equal to "Parse error: Expected `[names | names …]`, found [ | k ih; rfl".

## Test: a proof resting on its own axiom is admitted, not verified

Let v be kernelVerdict(recordedExit("admitted_axiom"), recordedReport("admitted_axiom"), false, "proof_of_goal", "goal").
Expect that v's kind is equal to "admitted_axiom".
Expect that v's axioms is equal to ["zero_add_axiom"].
Expect that v's detail is equal to "every block checked, but the proof rests on zero_add_axiom, outside propext, Quot_sound and Classical_choice".

## Test: the kernel alone would accept a shadowed goal, which is why names are probed

Let v be kernelVerdict(recordedExit("shadowed"), recordedReport("shadowed"), false, "proof_of_goal", "goal").
Expect that v's kind is equal to "verified".
Let shadow be "Definition goal : Prop := True.\n\nTheorem proof_of_goal : goal := by exact I.".
Expect that submissionProblems(shadow, "proof_of_goal", "goal") is equal to ["the submission redeclares the goal goal"].
Expect that probeOutcome(recordedExit("probe_bound"), recordedReport("probe_bound"), "goal") is equal to "bound".

## Test: a probe tells a bound name from a free one, and anything else from both

Expect that probeOutcome(recordedExit("probe_bound"), recordedReport("probe_bound"), "goal") is equal to "bound".
Expect that probeOutcome(recordedExit("probe_free"), recordedReport("probe_free"), "succ_step") is equal to "free".
Expect that probeOutcome(recordedExit("probe_free"), recordedReport("probe_free"), "other_name") is equal to "unknown".
Expect that probeOutcome(1, "segmentation fault", "x") is equal to "unknown".

## Test: one bound name rejects a submission, and an unanswered probe is infrastructure

Inspect nameProbeVerdict("submission", "the statement or the prelude", ["succ_step", "goal"], ["free", "bound"]):
    When Some (v):
        Expect that v's kind is equal to "rejected".
        Expect that v's error is equal to "the submission declares goal, which the statement or the prelude already binds".
    When None:
        Expect that "a verdict" is equal to "none".
Inspect nameProbeVerdict("submission", "the statement or the prelude", ["succ_step"], ["unknown"]):
    When Some (v):
        Expect that v's kind is equal to "infrastructure".
    When None:
        Expect that "a verdict" is equal to "none".
Expect that nameProbeVerdict("submission", "the statement or the prelude", ["succ_step", "proof_of_goal"], ["free", "free"]) is none.

## Test: a deadline, a non-report and an exit that contradicts its report are infrastructure

Expect that (kernelVerdict(0, recordedReport("verified"), true, "proof_of_goal", "goal"))'s kind is equal to "infrastructure".
Expect that (kernelVerdict(101, "thread 'main' panicked", false, "proof_of_goal", "goal"))'s kind is equal to "infrastructure".
Expect that (kernelVerdict(1, recordedReport("verified"), false, "proof_of_goal", "goal"))'s kind is equal to "infrastructure".
Expect that (kernelVerdict(0, recordedReport("rejected"), false, "proof_of_goal", "goal"))'s kind is equal to "infrastructure".
Expect that (kernelVerdict(0, "{{\"blocks\":[],\"checked\":true}}", false, "proof_of_goal", "goal"))'s kind is equal to "infrastructure".

## Test: a theorem of another type does not pass the closing Check

Let v be kernelVerdict(recordedExit("verified"), recordedReport("verified"), false, "proof_of_goal", "other_goal").
Expect that v's kind is equal to "rejected".
Expect that v's block is equal to 7.
Expect that v's error is equal to "`Check proof_of_goal.` printed `proof_of_goal : goal`, not `proof_of_goal : other_goal`".

## Test: a report whose block numbers skip is not a report

Inspect parseKernelReport("{{\"blocks\":[{{\"block\":2,\"output\":\"\"}}],\"checked\":true,\"error\":null,\"failed_block\":null,\"file\":\"f\",\"surface\":\"kernel_document\"}}"):
    When Ok (r):
        Expect that r's checked is equal to false.
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "the report numbers block 2 where 1 belongs".

## Test: a proof document is bound to the statement it begins with

Let doc be fixtureStatement().
Let st be a new Statement with id "stmt:x" and problemId "p" and document doc and sha256 sha256Hex(doc) and goalName "goal" and route "C" and reviewState "accepted" and author "c" and model "m" and createdAt 0.
Expect that boundToStatement(st, assembleProofDocument(doc, fixtureProof(), "proof_of_goal")) is equal to true.
Expect that boundToStatement(st, assembleProofDocument(doc + "\n\nDefinition extra : Nat := Zero.", fixtureProof(), "proof_of_goal")) is equal to false.
Let mutable stale be st.
Set stale's sha256 to sha256Hex("another statement").
Expect that boundToStatement(stale, assembleProofDocument(doc, fixtureProof(), "proof_of_goal")) is equal to false.

## Test: each embedded report is the recorded file, byte for byte

This test may use the real filesystem.
Repeat for fixture in ["verified", "rejected", "admitted_axiom", "parse_error", "shadowed", "classical", "probe_bound", "probe_free"]:
    Inspect read("tests/fixtures/kernel/" + fixture + ".prove.json"):
        When Ok (text):
            Expect that trimEnd(text) is equal to recordedReport(fixture).
        When Err (e):
            Expect that e is equal to "readable " + fixture.
    Inspect read("tests/fixtures/kernel/" + fixture + ".check.json"):
        When Ok (text):
            Expect that trimEnd(text) is equal to recordedReport(fixture).
        When Err (e):
            Expect that e is equal to "readable " + fixture.
    Inspect read("tests/fixtures/kernel/" + fixture + ".exit"):
        When Ok (text):
            Expect that parseInt(trim(text)) is equal to recordedExit(fixture).
        When Err (e):
            Expect that e is equal to "readable " + fixture.

## Test: the assembled fixture documents are the recorded ones

This test may use the real filesystem.
Inspect read("tests/fixtures/kernel/verified.lg"):
    When Ok (text):
        Expect that text is equal to assembleProofDocument(fixtureStatement(), fixtureProof(), "proof_of_goal").
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "readable".
Inspect read("tests/fixtures/kernel/rejected.lg"):
    When Ok (text):
        Expect that text is equal to assembleProofDocument(fixtureStatement(), "Theorem proof_of_goal : goal := by intro n; rfl.", "proof_of_goal").
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "readable".
